# Repository convert then map

`Read` / `ReadSingle` (and the write reverse path) have **two concerns**. Keep them as separate pipeline steps. Do not fold mapping into the converter or conversion into the mapper.

1. **Convert** — `rowConverter` / `RowTypeConverter`: database cell types and flat column → `T` (reflection / metadata).
2. **Map** — `Mapper` / `IMapper<T, T>`: reshape the already-converted object (nested contacts, derived fields). Default mapper is identity.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — mapper owns Row→T, converter skipped or inlined
yield return Mapper.Map(reader.Current);
new RowTypeMapper<T>(rowConverter) // as the only Read step

// ✅ GOOD — convert db types, then map to objects
yield return Mapper.Map(rowConverter.Convert(reader.Current ?? throw ...));
// writes: rowConverter.ReverseConvert(Mapper.ReverseMap(item))
```

Same split in TypeScript (`rowConverter.convert` then `mapper.map`) and Rust (`row_converter.convert` then `IMapper::map`).
